WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.793
This video is for the person who looks after the Report Builder:

00:00:04.793 --> 00:00:08.749
who may build and see reports, how to move reports to another site,

00:00:08.749 --> 00:00:13.410
what the limits mean on large data, and what to do when something does not work.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:21.189
Open Access Control, Roles, and edit a role.

00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:24.267
Search its permissions for custom reports.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:29.397
Build reports and manage own custom reports and views lets a person design

00:00:29.397 --> 00:00:33.053
reports and views, and change and delete their own.

00:00:33.505 --> 00:00:38.417
View all custom reports lets a person run every report, whoever owns it.

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:43.582
Manage all custom reports and views lets them change and delete every report

00:00:43.582 --> 00:00:47.235
and view, and it includes the two permissions above.

00:00:47.686 --> 00:00:52.374
Share custom reports publicly and through share links is the one that lets

00:00:52.374 --> 00:00:56.946
a person share a report with the Anonymous role, and create share links.

00:00:57.405 --> 00:00:59.361
Search for report groups.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:05.859
Manage report groups lets a person create, change and delete the groups reports are listed under.

00:01:05.859 --> 00:01:09.265
Manage all custom reports and views includes it.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:18.295
This is the Reports menu of a person whose role has none of these permissions.

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:22.440
It lists the reports they may run, but there is no Report Builder.

00:01:24.126 --> 00:01:30.056
In the role, tick Build reports and manage own custom reports and views, and save.

00:01:31.616 --> 00:01:37.052
Now the same person has Report Builder under Reports, and builds reports of their own.

00:01:37.052 --> 00:01:41.956
They see their own reports, and the ones shared with them, and no one else's.

00:01:46.135 --> 00:01:49.079
To bring reports onto a site, import them.

00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:54.477
Under Tools, Deployments, JSON Import takes a recipe with the Report Designs step,

00:01:54.477 --> 00:01:58.035
and Package Import takes the same in a package file.

00:01:58.487 --> 00:01:59.606
Click Import.

00:01:59.606 --> 00:02:02.846
The import matches each report by its identifier:

00:02:02.846 --> 00:02:07.146
a report that exists is replaced, and one that does not is created,

00:02:07.146 --> 00:02:09.797
so the same file can be imported again.

00:02:09.797 --> 00:02:11.977
Share links are never imported.

00:02:12.429 --> 00:02:16.151
The reports and their groups are now in the Report Builder.

00:02:16.151 --> 00:02:19.931
Each one keeps its owner when a user with the same user name

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:24.569
exists on the site, and belongs to the person who ran the import otherwise.

00:02:28.769 --> 00:02:33.039
The builder reads each data set in batches and never holds a whole

00:02:33.039 --> 00:02:34.522
data set in memory.

00:02:34.522 --> 00:02:39.979
Big joins and totals use temporary files on the server, so they are slower, not wrong.

00:02:40.729 --> 00:02:44.492
A report that reads more rows than the limit says so with a

00:02:44.492 --> 00:02:47.908
warning, and the numbers cover only the rows it read.

00:02:47.908 --> 00:02:51.961
Add a shorter period or another filter, or ask for the limits to

00:02:51.961 --> 00:02:54.509
be raised in the site's configuration.

00:02:55.259 --> 00:02:59.331
A new report starts with the last 30 days of its main date.

00:02:59.331 --> 00:03:03.403
For big data, keep a date filter on every report, and use a

00:03:03.403 --> 00:03:06.849
scheduled view for data that is heavy to prepare.

00:03:11.049 --> 00:03:13.269
No Report Builder under Reports:

00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:17.417
the feature may be off, or the person lacks the build permission.

00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:21.389
People who only run shared reports see Shared Reports instead.

00:03:22.139 --> 00:03:24.308
Fewer records than expected:

00:03:24.308 --> 00:03:28.007
the date filter of a new report is the last 30 days.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:30.559
Pick a longer period, or All time.

00:03:31.309 --> 00:03:33.649
Totals too high after a join:

00:03:33.649 --> 00:03:36.457
a join repeats a row for each match.

00:03:36.457 --> 00:03:41.939
Count distinct values, or sum from the data set that has one row per record.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:46.266
A shared report shows data its viewer cannot open:

00:03:46.266 --> 00:03:50.610
that is expected, since it reads data with its owner's access.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:53.229
Share only what viewers should see.

00:03:55.229 --> 00:03:59.699
Give the five permissions with care, move reports with a deployment plan, and

00:03:59.699 --> 00:04:01.799
keep a date filter on large data.

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:03.199
Thanks for watching.

